## Phase 9: Preserve overlapping tiles during map view changes

Depends on Phases 5–8.

Outcome: panning and zooming retain valid presentation and GPU inputs for tiles that remain visible, without disappearing and reappearing solely because the visible set changed.

- [x] Replace whole-view receipt clearing and pending-request dropping with incremental entering/retained/leaving tile handling. Retain valid receipts and useful in-flight work for overlapping tiles; request newly visible or genuinely invalidated inputs. Update screen placement and zoom independently of environmental input validity.
- [x] Separate world/purge/source validity from view membership. Cancel or deprioritize work that left the view without revoking still-needed work; admit late completions only when their source provenance is current and the tile is applicable to the current view. Preserve current explored-coverage checks immediately before drawing.
- [x] Protect retained visible regional/tile snapshots, bundles and GPU resources during view transitions. Remove or evict off-view entries before unchanged overlapping entries as needed; prevent admission order or cache shrink from causing eviction/reload cascades. Keep retention and queue admission bounded under explicit policies; do not add speculative prefetch or remote retrieval.
- [x] Reuse unchanged regional, elevation, coverage and ocean-classification textures across scrolling and zooming. Re-read or upload only newly needed, changed or legitimately evicted inputs. Preserve targeted regional/tile invalidation, normal per-frame GPU comparison and rendering, and shared-pass state ownership.
- [x] Retain close/reopen, tab/minimap eligibility, shader reload, purge, world-switch and shutdown behavior. Stopping disposable presentation must still preserve pending environmental writes and reject stale world/purge results.
- [x] Add focused regressions for partially overlapping pans in both directions, rapid leave/re-entry, zoom/view shrink, unchanged tile sets with changed screen positions, and views larger than cache floors. Verify unchanged overlapping tiles keep their receipts/source identities, remain drawable without reacquisition gaps, and incur no unnecessary local reads or texture uploads. Cover queued completions, source/ocean updates and stale coverage independently.
- [x] Use subagents for focused tests and canonical build/package checks. Verify stable scrolling through the normal map/RenderDoc workflow without permanent diagnostic readbacks or a standalone graphics harness. Reconcile [HabitatEvaluation.md](HabitatEvaluation.md), proposal performance/lifecycle requirements and Integration contracts 7–8. Leave representative resource/frame-time measurement to Phase 10.

