Actual-frame atlas uploads are zero both before and inside the habitat pass. The 9 glTexImage2D and 213 glTexSubImage2D entries preceding the frame's first structured chunk (51440) are RenderDoc resource-initialization reconstruction, not upload work performed during this captured frame; they are excluded from frame-cost counts. This steady frame demonstrates reuse, while focused tests/source review cover new/changed partial uploads. Atlas occupancy, payload and binding improvements do not resolve per-tile submission, upload-state batching, view CPU work or overall zoom-out lag; those remain in 9.4–9.9 and Phase 10.

Captured first-draw pipeline state confirms linear regional filtering, nearest terrain filtering, ClampToEdge and no mip filtering, with sampler objects zero so texture parameters apply. Parsed uniforms agree with first-draw reflection. All 8,304 world tile origins are unique; all sampled allocation origins are aligned and in bounds. No high/medium RenderDoc debug message appears. These checks and the user's visual confirmation support current rendering behavior without claiming an exhaustive hardware-precision test.

A TEMP-only non-graphics experiment using the exact current Release internal types reproduces this captured 8,304-terrain/48-regional workload and its staged page-capacity history: three terrain pages with 8,316 cells and six regional pages with 61 cells. The measured graph includes HabitatAtlas/page/layout/slot ownership, GpuRegionalTextures/GpuTileTextures, EnvironmentalInput leases and source-keyed BoundedLru entries. LRUs protect the complete visible set before admission, matching production behavior rather than allocating off-view candidate nodes. Shared packed payloads/layouts/epoch and a singleton non-recording backend are warmed outside measurement. After 20 warm runs, five measured runs each allocate 3,085,984 bytes; GC.GetTotalMemory(true) with KeepAlive yields a stable retained managed-heap estimate of 2,219,144 bytes. Elapsed times are 2.9470, 3.1932, 2.9673, 3.9582 and 3.2173 ms (median 3.1932 ms). Allocated bytes include dictionary growth and transient native-constructor data; the retained figure is a scoped managed estimate, not the game's live heap. Source payloads, shader/mesh/database/preparation caches, driver storage and real GL execution are excluded. This records atlas metadata costs without substituting a synthetic result for live frame-time acceptance.

